Check how dsymutil finds the dSYM of a merged library, and that without a
usable one, the object files of the library are linked instead.

The inputs are those of mergeable-libs-relocation-map.test, plus a _debug
build variant of libfoo, which is built at -O0 under the same install name,
and merged with libbar into libvariant:

$ cd llvm/test/tools/dsymutil
$ D=Inputs/mergeable-libs/dwarf5
$ LINK="clang -target arm64-apple-macos15 -dynamiclib \
    -Wl,-oso_prefix,$(pwd -P)/ -Wl,-segalign,0x1000"
$ clang -target arm64-apple-macos15 -isysroot / -g -gdwarf-5 -O0 \
    -fdebug-compilation-dir=/tmp -c Inputs/mergeable-libs/foo.c \
    -o $D/foo_debug.o
$ ZERO_AR_DATE=1 $LINK -Wl,-make_mergeable \
    -install_name /path/to/libfoo.dylib $D/foo_debug.o -o $D/libfoo_debug.dylib
$ ZERO_AR_DATE=1 $LINK $D/client.o -Wl,-merge_library,$D/libfoo_debug.dylib \
    -Wl,-merge_library,$D/libbar.dylib -o $D/libvariant.dylib

DEFINE: %{in} = %p/../Inputs/mergeable-libs/dwarf5
DEFINE: %{dsymutil} = dsymutil -oso-prepend-path=%p/..
DEFINE: %{map} = Contents/Resources/Relocations/aarch64

RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t

A variant has its own DWARF and relocation map in the dSYM of the library,
which are used before those of the library itself. libbar has no variant.
Search paths without the dSYMs are skipped silently.

RUN: %{dsymutil} %{in}/libfoo.dylib -o %t/dsyms/libfoo.dylib.dSYM
RUN: %{dsymutil} %{in}/libfoo_debug.dylib -o %t/dsyms/libfoo.dylib.dSYM
RUN: %{dsymutil} %{in}/libbar.dylib -o %t/dsyms/libbar.dylib.dSYM
RUN: %{dsymutil} -build-variant-suffix=_debug -D %t/nowhere -D %t/dsyms \
RUN:   %{in}/libvariant.dylib -o %t/variant.dSYM 2>&1 | count 0
RUN: llvm-dwarfdump --debug-info %t/variant.dSYM \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VARIANT

VARIANT:      DW_AT_name ("Inputs/mergeable-libs/foo.c")
VARIANT:      DW_AT_APPLE_origin ("/path/to/libfoo.dylib")
VARIANT:      DW_TAG_subprogram
VARIANT-NEXT:   DW_AT_low_pc (0x00000000000004f4)
VARIANT:        DW_AT_name ("foo")
VARIANT:      DW_TAG_formal_parameter
VARIANT-NEXT:   DW_AT_location (DW_OP_breg31 WSP+8)
VARIANT:      DW_AT_name ("Inputs/mergeable-libs/bar.c")
VARIANT:      DW_AT_APPLE_origin ("/path/to/libbar.dylib")
VARIANT:      DW_TAG_subprogram
VARIANT-NEXT:   DW_AT_low_pc (0x0000000000000574)
VARIANT:        DW_AT_name ("bar")

Without the dSYM of libbar, its object file is linked. libbar comes after
libfoo, whose dSYM is found, and must not get the symbols of libbar.

RUN: %{dsymutil} %{in}/libfoo.dylib -o %t/onlyfoo/libfoo.dylib.dSYM
RUN: %{dsymutil} -D %t/onlyfoo %{in}/libclient.dylib -o %t/nobar.dSYM 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NOBAR-WARN --implicit-check-not=warning
RUN: llvm-dwarfdump --debug-info %t/nobar.dSYM \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NOBAR

NOBAR-WARN: warning: (arm64) /path/to/libbar.dylib no usable dSYM of the library was found in the dSYM search paths, linking its object files instead

NOBAR:      DW_AT_name ("Inputs/mergeable-libs/foo.c")
NOBAR:      DW_AT_APPLE_origin ("/path/to/libfoo.dylib")
NOBAR:      DW_TAG_subprogram
NOBAR-NEXT:   DW_AT_low_pc (0x00000000000004f4)
NOBAR:        DW_AT_name ("foo")
NOBAR:      DW_AT_name ("Inputs/mergeable-libs/bar.c")
NOBAR-NOT:  DW_AT_APPLE_origin
NOBAR:      DW_TAG_variable
NOBAR-NEXT:   DW_AT_name ("bar_counter")
NOBAR:        DW_AT_location (DW_OP_addr 0x1028)
NOBAR:      DW_TAG_subprogram
NOBAR-NEXT:   DW_AT_low_pc (0x0000000000000558)
NOBAR:        DW_AT_name ("bar")

A merged library has an N_LIB entry for each of its object files: the missing
dSYM of libclient is reported once, and its three object files are linked.

RUN: %{dsymutil} -D %t/nowhere %{in}/libtop.dylib -o %t/noclient.dSYM 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NOCLIENT-WARN --implicit-check-not=warning
RUN: llvm-dwarfdump --debug-info %t/noclient.dSYM \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NOCLIENT \
RUN:       --implicit-check-not=DW_AT_APPLE_origin

NOCLIENT-WARN: warning: (arm64) /path/to/libclient.dylib no usable dSYM of the library was found in the dSYM search paths, linking its object files instead

NOCLIENT:      DW_AT_name ("Inputs/mergeable-libs/top.c")
NOCLIENT:      DW_AT_name ("Inputs/mergeable-libs/client.c")
NOCLIENT:      DW_TAG_subprogram
NOCLIENT-NEXT:   DW_AT_low_pc (0x00000000000004e0)
NOCLIENT:        DW_AT_name ("display")
NOCLIENT:      DW_AT_name ("Inputs/mergeable-libs/foo.c")
NOCLIENT:      DW_TAG_subprogram
NOCLIENT-NEXT:   DW_AT_low_pc (0x000000000000050c)
NOCLIENT:        DW_AT_name ("foo")
NOCLIENT:      DW_AT_name ("Inputs/mergeable-libs/bar.c")
NOCLIENT:      DW_TAG_subprogram
NOCLIENT-NEXT:   DW_AT_low_pc (0x0000000000000570)
NOCLIENT:        DW_AT_name ("bar")

A dSYM is unusable without the relocations to merge its debug info: when its
relocation map has none, as older dsymutils wrote for DWARF 5, or when the
relocations could not be in its DWARF.

RUN: %{dsymutil} %{in}/libfoo.dylib -o %t/bad/libfoo.dylib.dSYM
RUN: %{dsymutil} %{in}/libbar.dylib -o %t/bad/libbar.dylib.dSYM
RUN: cp %t/empty.yml %t/bad/libfoo.dylib.dSYM/%{map}/libfoo.dylib.yml
RUN: cp %t/oversized.yml %t/bad/libbar.dylib.dSYM/%{map}/libbar.dylib.yml
RUN: %{dsymutil} -D %t/bad %{in}/libclient.dylib -o %t/bad.dSYM 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BAD-WARN --implicit-check-not=warning
RUN: llvm-dwarfdump --debug-info %t/bad.dSYM \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BAD --implicit-check-not=DW_AT_APPLE_origin

BAD-WARN:      warning: (arm64) {{.*}}libfoo.dylib.yml relocation map file has no relocation
BAD-WARN-NEXT: warning: (arm64) /path/to/libfoo.dylib no usable dSYM of the library was found in the dSYM search paths, linking its object files instead
BAD-WARN-NEXT: warning: (arm64) {{.*}}libbar.dylib.yml relocation map file does not match the DWARF of the dSYM
BAD-WARN-NEXT: warning: (arm64) /path/to/libbar.dylib no usable dSYM of the library was found in the dSYM search paths, linking its object files instead

BAD:      DW_AT_name ("Inputs/mergeable-libs/foo.c")
BAD:      DW_TAG_subprogram
BAD-NEXT:   DW_AT_low_pc (0x00000000000004f4)
BAD:        DW_AT_name ("foo")
BAD:      DW_AT_name ("Inputs/mergeable-libs/bar.c")
BAD:      DW_TAG_subprogram
BAD-NEXT:   DW_AT_low_pc (0x0000000000000558)
BAD:        DW_AT_name ("bar")

#--- empty.yml
---
triple:          'arm64-apple-darwin'
binary-path:     libfoo.dylib
relocations:     []
...
#--- oversized.yml
---
triple:          'arm64-apple-darwin'
binary-path:     libbar.dylib
relocations:
  - { offset: 0x8, size: 0x40, addend: 0x0, symName: _bar, symBinAddr: 0x380, symSize: 0x18 }
...
